From a8a7ee5db33b68031323f4da6fa387bfb87b73b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josef Schlehofer <pepe.schlehofer@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 06:35:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic: 6.6: media: add pending fixes for DVB tuner
 hot-unplug

Unplugging an az6007 based DVB-C tuner, such as the TechniSat CableStar
Combo HD CI, while tvheadend uses it floods the log and the USB
disconnect does not complete. The CA thread spins on failed CAM status
polls, drxk keeps retrying I2C transfers on the gone device, and dmxdev
and dvb_ca wait for users that are never woken.

Add v2 of the series submitted upstream to pending-6.6. With it the
disconnect completes in about 150 ms and tvheadend picks the adapter up
again when it is plugged back in.

v1 was tested on a Turris 1.x (mpc85xx/p2020) with 6.18, v2 on a Turris
Omnia (mvebu) with Turris OS 9.1.2 and in QEMU with vidtv on v7.3-rc2.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261004100741.71711-1-pepe.schlehofer@gmail.com/
Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/25427
Signed-off-by: Josef Schlehofer <pepe.schlehofer@gmail.com>
